==Venue==
[[File:Windsor Park redevelopment .jpg|thumb|275px|[[Windsor Park]] in [[Belfast]] hosted the match.]]

The match was the first UEFA club competition final to be played in Northern Ireland. The 18,500-capacity [[Windsor Park]] is the home of [[Linfield F.C.|Linfield]] and the [[Northern Ireland national football team|Northern Ireland national team]]. Opened in 1905, the stadium was most recently renovated from 2014 to 2016 with aid from UEFA's HatTrick assistance programme.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/026c-12f8d0f47b0b-b19edf527c7f-1000/ |title=Northern Ireland's big moment arrives with UEFA support |publisher=UEFA |date=11 August 2021 |access-date=7 May 2022}}</ref> The venue previously hosted the finals of the [[2005 UEFA European Under-19 Championship]] and [[2017 UEFA Women's Under-19 Championship]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/0255-0d939ff4f94d-66ebd547547f-1000/ |title=2021 Super Cup to take place in Belfast |publisher=UEFA |date=9 August 2021 |access-date=7 May 2022}}</ref>

===Host selection===
An open bidding process was launched on 28 September 2018 by UEFA to select the venues of the finals of the UEFA Champions League, UEFA Europa League, and UEFA Women's Champions League in 2021. Associations had until 26 October 2018 to express interest, and bid dossiers must be submitted by 15 February 2019.

UEFA announced on 1 November 2018 that four associations had expressed interest in hosting the 2021 UEFA Super Cup,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0250-0c5119fbc7e9-b9de0907b594-1000--11-associations-interested-in-hosting-2021-club-finals/|title=11 associations interested in hosting 2021 club finals|publisher=UEFA|date=1 November 2018}}</ref> and on 22 February 2019 that all four associations submitted their dossiers by the deadline.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/024e-0f8e68aa43f5-6b3adef08395-1000--9-associations-bidding-to-host-2021-club-finals/|title=9 associations bidding to host 2021 club finals|publisher=[[UEFA]]|date=22 February 2019}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.uefa.com/printoutfiles/competitions/uefasupercup/2021/e/e_2030316_pk.pdf|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210810124641/https://www.uefa.com/printoutfiles/competitions/uefasupercup/2021/e/e_2030316_pk.pdf|url-status=dead|archive-date=10 August 2021|title=Match Press Kit|date=10 August 2021|work=[[UEFA]]|access-date= 10 August 2021}}</ref>

